{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530057-v5-mostly-protestant-hunters","id":1530057,"title":"(V5, mostly) Protestant hunters?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-05T16:08:23-08:00","id":1530057,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> (V5, mostly) Protestant hunters?","content":"I'm working more on this chronicle I just started, and to the best of my memory I don't recall much if anything published about Protestant hunters and hunter organizations. Knowing fully I could be mistaken, I thought I'd ask here in case I might have missed something. I'm definitely not going the &quot;Hellsing&quot; route on this, but due to my chronicle, the city's history, and demography, the Second Inquisition would consist of Protestants -- specifically, evangelical Christians -- rather than Catholics (in fact, Catholic hunters and Inquisitors have more or less left the city to rot).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-05T16:21:29-08:00","id":1530058,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s some material about the Long Night in Requiem which could be adapted to a Masquerade chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-05T17:24:05-08:00","id":1530060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530057-v5-mostly-protestant-hunters#post1530057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm working more on this chronicle I just started, and to the best of my memory I don't recall much if anything published about Protestant hunters and hunter organizations. Knowing fully I could be mistaken, I thought I'd ask here in case I might have missed something. I'm definitely not going the &quot;Hellsing&quot; route on this, but due to my chronicle, the city's history, and demography, the Second Inquisition would consist of Protestants -- specifically, evangelical Christians -- rather than Catholics (in fact, Catholic hunters and Inquisitors have more or less left the city to rot).</div> </div> </div> </div>There's actually a few noted Protestant hunters in the Classic World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> In terms of groups, there's the Anglican Knights of Saint George, though they are fairly obscure.<br /> <br /> But in terms of Low Church Protestants/Calvinists and Evangelicals, you've got quite a few, especially in the early days but they were largely lone wolves or local groups.<br /> <br /> Caiaphas Smith from the original <i>The Hunters Hunted </i>is a Puritan with insane levels of True Faith who ghouled himself solely so he could live long enough to kill more vampires. In V5, he could very well be a general within the Second Inquisition.<br /> <br /> In <i>The Inquisition</i> (a book from 2e that was part of the &quot;Year of the Hunter&quot; promotion) one of the templates for player characters is &quot;The Puritan&quot;, who is an Evangelical Neo-Puritan that is anti-Catholic but is begrudgingly working alongside the Society of Leopold to gain more information on vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-05T18:52:39-08:00","id":1530068,"title":"","content":"Technically more sorcerers/linear mages than hunters per se, but i remembered <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Nephite_Priesthood\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> group and also <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Seven_Thunders\" target=\"_blank\">a more obscure one</a>.<br /> Both could work pretty fine alongside the 2nd Inquisition i guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-05T21:48:03-08:00","id":1530077,"title":"","content":"For inspiration on Protestant &quot;witch hunters&quot;, I would go to historical figures like Matthew Hopkins (the Witchfinder General) and fictional figures like Solomon Kane (whom the NPC of Caiphas Smith - and Sullivan Dane - is clearly based on). Both are Puritans, and thus good figures for low-Church Protestants. If you want to go outside the Anglophone world, there are plenty of Protestant witch trials in the 17th century you can research. Just update that mentality to the modern day.<br /> <br /> If you want more directly American inspiration, you can use stories like those of Manly Wade Wellman's Silver John (about a roving hillbilly balladeer in Appalachia who fights demons and monsters) who would be a witch hunter, although definitely not someone ordained. Or use any number of preachers leading congregations who are portrayed as against corruption like the characters of Billy and Cassie St. Cyr from Justified.<br /> <br /> I would probably make any Protestant witch hunters be individuals or in small, local groups, rather than in large institutions like the Society of Saint Leopold. They'll be based around charismatic and &quot;blessed&quot; witch hunters working on their own and recruiting from victims' families rather than from any organizational support. In fact, although Abraham Van Helsing is clearly Catholic, it would be easy to turn him and the group of hunters in Dracula into a Protestant style witch hunting group. Probably everyone else in that group - Holmwood, Quincy, Seward, the Harkers - are Protestant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-05T23:49:22-08:00","id":1530080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530057-v5-mostly-protestant-hunters?p=1530058#post1530058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There\u2019s some material about the Long Night in Requiem which could be adapted to a Masquerade chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be more precise, the Long Night are a Hunter the Vigil group - apocalyptic evangelicals, specifically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T16:41:29-08:00","id":1530225,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the replies. I don't really need inspiration for it as I know where I'm going with it. Long story short: Louisville, KY, is home to one of the biggest megachurches in the US. It's also a thirty-minute straight shot down a major state road from Fort Knox, and a three-hour drive down a couple interstates from Fort Campbell. Fort Knox, not the big show here: Campbell is, given it's the home of the 101st Airborne and a couple major Army special forces units, specifically one which specializes in operations in the Middle East. <br /> <br /> So, the megachurch is the eyes, ears, and payroll for the Inquisition in Louisville, and these special forces operators are the muscle. They're (as of yet) unconnected to Second Inquisition in federal law enforcement or intelligence, nor are they connected to the Catholic church (because you know, pickledick evangelical conservative megachurchies). So, fantastic ground game (at least in the affluent, white, parts of town) and unparalleled capability to drop the hammer on a lick, but diddly squat in terms of faith and severely lacking in the infosec/electronic warfare department. They're also connected (through a few layers of shell corporations, a <i>lot</i> of money laundering, and corrupt but publicly pious politicians) to a police/government gentrification conspiracy, but that's neither here nor there.<br /> <br /> I just wanted to know if that tracks with what's been written about protestant hunters so far. I kind of want to diverge from the usual, which tends to be lone wolf Van Helsing and/or small fundamentalist True Faith-y types staging the vampire hunter equivalent to snatch-and-run attacks, and build an informal organization that actually wages conflicts more similarly to how the Camarilla is narrated to in the revised GttC -- land grabs, narrative control, surgical raids against identified high-value targets, strategic area denial, and the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T10:56:51-08:00","id":1530290,"title":"","content":"&quot;<i>Let the streets run red</i>&quot; has the <b>Night's Cross</b>, which is definitely more organized and militant than what you wanted, but has the kind of background that you were interested into: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Night%27s_Cross\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Night%27s_Cross</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}